642,453.744263,371.168060,443.797119,560.457642,443.797119,322.808838,441.781921,560.480286,441.781921,322.808838,431.834839,560.480286,431.834839,322.808838,429.819641,560.440247,429.819641,322.808838,419.872498,560.440247,419.872498,322.808838,417.914124,347.484009,417.914124,322.808838,407.966980,347.484009,407.966980,347.230408,417.914124,375.031616,417.914124,347.230408,410.131470,375.031616,410.131470,374.796814,417.914368,400.942596,417.914368,374.796814,407.266510,400.942596,407.266510,403.410065,417.914368,420.243042,418.217194,403.410065,407.967224,420.243042,407.967224,420.263824,418.754395,471.208130,418.754395,420.263824,407.967224,471.208130,407.967224,473.661377,417.914368,560.437866,417.914368,473.661377,407.967224,560.437866,407.967224,322.809052,405.952026,560.397400,405.952026,322.809052,396.004944,560.397400,396.004944,322.809052,393.989746,560.449463,393.989746,322.809052,384.042603,560.449463,384.042603,322.809052,382.027405,560.378723,382.027405,322.809052,372.080322,560.378723,372.080322,322.809052,370.065125,560.457520,370.065125,322.809052,360.117981,560.457520,360.117981,322.809052,358.102783,560.425781,358.102783,322.809052,348.155701,560.425781,348.155701,322.809021,346.140503,538.280273,346.140503,322.809021,336.193359,538.280273,336.193359,424.339661,613.375427,424.339661,621.101318,430.585327,613.375427,430.585327,621.101318,421.078156,611.154175,322.809387,611.154175,421.078156,621.101318,322.809387,621.101318,560.466797,623.116455,322.809387,623.116455,560.466797,633.063599,322.809387,633.063599,560.494324,635.078735,322.809387,635.078735,560.494324,645.025879,322.809387,645.025879,560.490601,647.041016,322.809387,647.041016,560.490601,656.988159,322.809387,656.988159,560.487244,659.003296,322.809387,659.003296,560.487244,668.950439,322.809387,668.950439" rect="322.497986,335.882507,560.837891,669.261292" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This study analyzed whether SJFT performance could be&#xD;predicted by physical fitness variables, derived from anaerobic&#xD;and aerobic metabolisms. This study has 4 main applications: (a)&#xD;total number of throws during SJFT was predicted by&#xD;physiological (upper-body V_&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-9.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>O</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>2</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>peak, ml$min</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>21</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>$kg</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>21</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>) and performance&#xD;variables (MP during Wingate test), indicating that&#xD;coaches who want to improve their athletes’ total number of&#xD;throws should design training programs to improve both upperbody&#xD;aerobic power and anaerobic capacity. Considering that&#xD;high-intensity interval training has been recommended to&#xD;achieve these adaptations, strength and conditioning professionals&#xD;should consider using sprint interval training protocols to&#xD;achieve such goal; (b) HR immediately after SJFTwas predicted&#xD;by upper-body (HRmax) and lower-body physiological variables&#xD;(HR at OBLA), suggesting that this variable can be achieved&#xD;through training protocols more directed to improve aerobic&#xD;power and capacity; (c) HR 1 minute after SJFT was explained&#xD;by upper-body (HRmax) and lower-body physiological variables&#xD;([La</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>21</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>]</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>peak</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>), indicating a need to use training protocols directed&#xD;to aerobic power training that could result in decreased blood&#xD;lactate for a given load; (d) SJFT index was explained only by&#xD;upper-bodyV_&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-9.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>O</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>2</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>peak (ml$min</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>21</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>$kg</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>21</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.7pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>), suggesting that training&#xD;protocols used to improve aerobic power are probably the best&#xD;approach to reduce the SJFT index. This can be achieved&#xD;through high-intensity interval training using long and short&#xD;intervals with intensities near MAP intensities. These predictors&#xD;show the importance of physical fitness variables, especially&#xD;upper-body, during the SJFT performed by judo athletes.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
